<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbeks to sell 40 pct stake in big metals combine.</title>
<headline>Uzbeks to sell 40 pct stake in big metals combine.</headline>
<dateline>ALMALYK, Uzbekistan 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan will hold a tender for a 40 percent stake in its big Almalyk base and precious metals plant to raise $400 million from foreign firms, the combine's head said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We got bids from South Korea's Daewoo Corp, U.S. company Gerald Metal SA, Switzerland's Glencore AG and a consortium of Germany's Thyssen Handelsunion, Siemens AG and Sweden's Svedala International AB,&quot; Vitaly Segedin told Reuters.</p>
</text>
